ui-enter-and-edit-text-in-filled-or-outlined-fields = Enter and edit text in filled or outlined fields.

ui-use-a-text-field-when-someone-needs-to-enter-text-into-a-ui-such-as-filling-in-contact-or = Use a text field when someone needs to enter text into a UI, such as filling in contact or payment information. Both variants of text fields use a container to provide a visual cue for interaction and provide the same functionality.

ui-outlined-text-fields = Outlined text fields

ui-outlined-text-fields-have-less-visual-emphasis-than-filled-text-fields-when-they-appear-in = Outlined text fields have less visual emphasis than filled text fields. When they appear in places like forms, where many text fields are placed together, their reduced emphasis helps simplify the layout.

ui-both-variants-of-text-field-provide-the-same-functionality-the-variant-used-can-depend-on = Both variants of text field provide the same functionality. The variant used can depend on style alone. Choose the variant that works best with an app's visual style, best accommodates the UI's goals, and is most distinct from other components and surrounding content.

ui-using-both-text-field-variants-on-the-same-screen = Using both text field variants on the same screen

ui-if-both-variants-of-text-field-are-used-in-a-ui-they-should-be-used-consistently-within-di = If both variants of text field are used in a UI, they should be used consistently within different sections, and not intermixed within the same region.

ui-for-compact-breakpoints-text-fields-can-span-the-full-width-of-the-display-for-medium-and = For compact breakpoints, text fields can span the full width of the display. For medium and expanded breakpoints, text fields should be bound by flexible margins or other containers, and should not span the full width of a large screen.

ui-dense-text-fields-enable-people-to-scan-and-take-action-on-large-amounts-of-information = Dense text fields enable people to scan and take action on large amounts of information.

ui-don-t-apply-density-to-text-fields-by-default-this-lowers-their-targets-below-the-recommen = Don't apply density to text fields by default. This lowers their targets below the recommended 48 × 48 CSS pixels. Instead, give people a way to choose a higher density. Keep all targets that revert the density setting at a minimum of 48 × 48 CSS pixels each.

