ui-containers-improve-the-discoverability-of-text-fields-by-creating-contrast-between-the-tex = Containers improve the discoverability of text fields by creating contrast between the text field and surrounding content. The container of an outlined text field has rounded corners, while the container of a filled text field has rounded top corners and square bottom corners.

ui-label-text-tells-people-what-information-is-requested-every-text-field-should-have-a-label = Label text tells people what information is requested. Every text field should have a label. Label text should be aligned with the input text and always visible. It shouldn't be truncated or take up multiple lines.

ui-a-text-field-doesn-t-require-a-label-if-the-field-s-purpose-is-indicated-by-a-separate-adj = A text field doesn't require a label if the field's purpose is indicated by a separate, adjacent label. Adjacent labels should be aligned to the leading edge of the text field container.

ui-full-name = Full name

ui-required-text-indicator = Required text indicator

ui-to-show-a-field-is-required-display-an-asterisk-next-to-the-label-text-and-explain-that-as = To show a field is required, display an asterisk (*) next to the label text, and explain that asterisks indicate required fields in supporting text or a single note at the beginning of the form. Indicate all required fields.

ui-input-text-is-text-a-person-has-entered-into-a-text-field-single-line-fields-display-only = Input text is text a person has entered into a text field. Single-line fields display only one line of text, multi-line fields grow to accommodate multiple lines, and text areas are fixed-height fields.

