ui-supporting-text-conveys-additional-information-about-the-input-field-such-as-how-it-will-b = Supporting text conveys additional information about the input field, such as how it will be used. If there is a character or word limit, include a counter that displays the ratio of characters used and the total limit.

ui-description = Description

ui-error-text = Error text

ui-for-text-fields-that-validate-their-content-such-as-passwords-replace-supporting-text-with = For text fields that validate their content, such as passwords, replace supporting text with error text. Swapping supporting text with error text prevents new lines of text from bumping content and changing the layout.

ui-error-icon = Error icon

ui-it-s-strongly-recommended-to-show-an-error-icon-when-the-text-field-is-in-the-error-state = It's strongly recommended to show an error icon when the text field is in the error state. This highlights the error for people with visual impairments and provides an additional sensory indicator.

